WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.139
Welcome to Module 2 of Global Secure
Access as the Identity-Aware Network:

2
00:00:05.139 --> 00:00:07.475
the client and Microsoft traffic.

3
00:00:07.475 --> 00:00:10.860
Everything after this module
depends on two things:

4
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:15.819
a client on every managed Windows
device, and the Microsoft traffic profile

5
00:00:15.819 --> 00:00:20.463
carrying that device's Microsoft three
sixty-five and Entra I D traffic.

6
00:00:20.463 --> 00:00:26.324
This module covers Steps 3 and 4 of the
Global Secure Access implementation guide.

7
00:00:26.324 --> 00:00:30.920
It takes about forty-five minutes,
plus a lab in your own test tenant.

8
00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:35.820
Why does this matter?

9
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.113
The client goes on every managed
Windows device, deployed by Intune,

10
00:00:40.113 --> 00:00:44.482
and opens a tunnel to the service edge
after the user signs in to Entra.

11
00:00:44.482 --> 00:00:49.583
How many devices actually carry it is the
first metric every later step leans on.

12
00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:54.684
The Microsoft traffic profile is what makes
the real source address visible to Entra

13
00:00:54.684 --> 00:00:57.988
I D, and it is the prerequisite
for the compliant network

14
00:00:57.988 --> 00:01:01.796
check and universal tenant
restrictions, which come in Module 3.

15
00:01:01.796 --> 00:01:05.272
So in this module you package
the client the way Learn does,

16
00:01:05.272 --> 00:01:09.111
scope the profile to a pilot group,
turn on source I P restoration,

17
00:01:09.111 --> 00:01:13.820
and measure how much of the pilot's
traffic the service actually carries.

18
00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:20.483
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module.

19
00:01:20.483 --> 00:01:23.427
You'll name the client's
platforms and prerequisites,

20
00:01:23.427 --> 00:01:25.769
and the configurations it doesn't support.

21
00:01:25.769 --> 00:01:29.574
You'll package it as a Win32 app
with Learn's install command,

22
00:01:29.574 --> 00:01:31.670
return codes and detection rule.

23
00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:36.027
You'll explain why D N S over H T
T P S is turned off in browsers,

24
00:01:36.027 --> 00:01:40.020
and why the hardening
remediation waits for ring two.

25
00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.922
You'll enable the Microsoft
traffic profile for a pilot group,

26
00:01:43.922 --> 00:01:45.682
with source I P restoration.

27
00:01:45.682 --> 00:01:50.058
And you'll compute client coverage, and
the share of sign-ins the service carries.

28
00:01:50.058 --> 00:01:52.898
You need Module 1, with the telemetry on,

29
00:01:52.898 --> 00:01:58.133
and a skim of Devices and Endpoints,
chapter four, for the Win32 app model.

30
00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:01.640
The lab runs in a test
tenant, never production.

31
00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:07.602
Unit 1 is where the client runs.

32
00:02:07.602 --> 00:02:12.548
Learn's client page: Windows ten L
T S C 2021 or later, Windows eleven,

33
00:02:12.548 --> 00:02:17.951
and Windows eleven on Arm, which has
a separate installer; Azure Virtual

34
00:02:17.951 --> 00:02:23.903
Desktop single-session and Windows three
sixty-five, but not A V D multi-session.

35
00:02:23.903 --> 00:02:26.513
It can't be installed
on a machine that hosts

36
00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:29.415
virtual machines with a
Hyper-V external switch.

37
00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:33.901
The device must be joined, hybrid
joined or registered in the tenant,

38
00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:37.265
and registered devices
carry only Private Access.

39
00:02:37.265 --> 00:02:43.471
The client tunnels I P version four only,
and it doesn't support secure D N S,

40
00:02:43.471 --> 00:02:49.677
D N S over T C P from browsers' built-in
resolvers, or Group Policy N R P T rules.

41
00:02:49.677 --> 00:02:53.220
Like the rest of the service,
it's available in G C C.

42
00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:56.408
Hosts it can't run on go
on the exception list,

43
00:02:56.408 --> 00:02:59.330
each with an owner and a review date.

44
00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:05.105
Unit 2 packages the client.

45
00:03:05.105 --> 00:03:09.470
Download it from the Global Secure
Access admin center, put it beside

46
00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:14.218
Learn's installation script, and wrap
both with the Win32 Content Prep Tool.

47
00:03:14.218 --> 00:03:17.277
Learn's script sets I P
version four preferred,

48
00:03:17.277 --> 00:03:22.268
runs the installer quietly, and returns
thirty ten when a restart is needed.

49
00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:26.668
Then create the Win32 app in
Intune with Learn's values.

50
00:03:26.668 --> 00:03:29.767
The install command runs the
script through PowerShell.

51
00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:35.343
The uninstall command runs the client with
uninstall, quiet and no-restart switches.

52
00:03:35.343 --> 00:03:37.179
Install behavior is System.

53
00:03:37.179 --> 00:03:39.767
The return codes are zero for success,

54
00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:43.855
thirty ten for a soft reboot,
and sixteen eighteen for retry.

55
00:03:43.855 --> 00:03:48.780
The detection rule is the client's file,
by version, at least the packaged version.

56
00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:51.897
And the assignment is
Required, to the pilot group,

57
00:03:51.897 --> 00:03:54.690
with the restart grace period enabled.

58
00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.178
Three more client decisions.

59
00:04:00.178 --> 00:04:04.140
First, D N S over H T T P S.

60
00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:07.041
The client doesn't support secure D N S,

61
00:04:07.041 --> 00:04:12.561
so an Intune settings catalog profile
sets Control the mode of D N S over

62
00:04:12.561 --> 00:04:17.427
H T T P S to Disabled, in Edge and
Chrome, assigned to the same group.

63
00:04:17.427 --> 00:04:19.003
Second, hardening.

64
00:04:19.003 --> 00:04:22.208
Learn's remediation scripts
can hide the disable and

65
00:04:22.208 --> 00:04:25.341
sign-out buttons and restrict
non-privileged users.

66
00:04:25.341 --> 00:04:30.676
Learn's advice is to let users run
unrestricted first and confirm nobody needs

67
00:04:30.676 --> 00:04:35.602
to disable the client, for a website or
a parallel V P N, before restricting.

68
00:04:35.602 --> 00:04:39.852
So the guide deploys the remediation
from ring two, not in the pilot.

69
00:04:39.852 --> 00:04:44.136
Third, upgrades, in rings: a
new app for each new version,

70
00:04:44.136 --> 00:04:49.102
assigned to a small group, widened,
and the old app deleted last.

71
00:04:49.102 --> 00:04:51.577
Rolling back re-assigns the previous app.

72
00:04:51.577 --> 00:04:58.310
And don't disable QUIC in browsers for
this; Step 5 handles QUIC, in Module 5.

73
00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:05.073
Unit 3 is the Microsoft traffic profile.

74
00:05:05.073 --> 00:05:09.459
It acquires Microsoft three
sixty-five and Entra I D traffic,

75
00:05:09.459 --> 00:05:14.197
and only this profile can; the
Internet Access profile never does.

76
00:05:14.197 --> 00:05:16.725
Enable it with Learn's Graph request,

77
00:05:16.725 --> 00:05:20.010
filtered on the m three
sixty-five traffic type.

78
00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:25.020
Then assign the pilot group in the admin
center, under traffic forwarding; the pages

79
00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:29.522
the guide read give no Graph request for
the assignment, so it's a portal step.

80
00:05:29.522 --> 00:05:30.909
Then set signaling.

81
00:05:30.909 --> 00:05:36.535
Signaling carries source I P restoration,
so Entra sees the user's real address.

82
00:05:36.535 --> 00:05:40.819
It's on by default only for tenants
that onboarded after June 2025,

83
00:05:40.819 --> 00:05:44.310
so the guide sets it explicitly
and records the state.

84
00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:47.372
It's also the setting the
compliant network check needs.

85
00:05:47.372 --> 00:05:52.509
And Learn's caution: once Conditional Access
policies depend on I P locations or the

86
00:05:52.509 --> 00:05:56.082
compliant network, turning
signaling off can block users,

87
00:05:56.082 --> 00:05:59.430
so those policies come
out of enforcement first.

88
00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:04.480
How do you know it works?

89
00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:09.099
The Microsoft traffic profile has no
report-only mode, so the pilot group

90
00:06:09.099 --> 00:06:13.642
is the audit phase, read through the
sign-in query for five business days.

91
00:06:13.642 --> 00:06:14.742
Three measures.

92
00:06:14.742 --> 00:06:18.692
Client coverage: the device usage
summary's active device count,

93
00:06:18.692 --> 00:06:21.971
divided by Intune's count of
in-scope Windows devices;

94
00:06:21.971 --> 00:06:26.218
the guide's starting target is
ninety-eight percent after ring three.

95
00:06:26.218 --> 00:06:30.966
Sign-ins through the service: the share
of sign-ins marked as through Global

96
00:06:30.966 --> 00:06:35.792
Secure Access, for in-scope users; the
starting target is ninety-five percent.

97
00:06:35.792 --> 00:06:40.366
And source I P restoration, by Learn's
deployment guide test: a SharePoint

98
00:06:40.366 --> 00:06:45.243
sign-in shows the same I P address with
the client running and with it disabled.

99
00:06:45.243 --> 00:06:50.130
The rollback is simple: remove the ring's
group from the profile's assignment.

100
00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:58.705
The lab runs in a test tenant, never
production, and the authors haven't run it.

101
00:06:58.705 --> 00:07:03.976
You need Module 1's lab done, one Windows
eleven test device joined to Entra I D,

102
00:07:03.976 --> 00:07:06.821
enrolled in Intune and in the pilot group,

103
00:07:06.821 --> 00:07:11.005
the client and Learn's script,
and the Win32 Content Prep Tool.

104
00:07:11.005 --> 00:07:14.143
Step one packages the
client in Command Prompt.

105
00:07:14.143 --> 00:07:19.919
Steps two and three are in Intune:
the Win32 app with Learn's values,

106
00:07:19.919 --> 00:07:24.092
and the D N S over H T T P
S profile; no hardening yet.

107
00:07:24.092 --> 00:07:26.124
Step four checks the pilot device:

108
00:07:26.124 --> 00:07:29.535
the file version should be
the packaged version or later,

109
00:07:29.535 --> 00:07:33.817
Disabled Components should read hex
twenty, I P version four preferred,

110
00:07:33.817 --> 00:07:36.430
and the four hardening
values aren't set yet.

111
00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:41.118
Open the client's health check, keep the
export, and the tray must read Connected.

112
00:07:41.118 --> 00:07:44.160
Step five asks Graph for
the device usage summary,

113
00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:47.120
which is the numerator of client coverage.

114
00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:53.815
Step six finds the
Microsoft traffic profile

115
00:07:53.815 --> 00:07:56.682
with Learn's filtered
request and enables it.

116
00:07:56.682 --> 00:08:00.544
This writes to the test tenant,
and Module 6 rolls it back.

117
00:08:00.544 --> 00:08:03.943
Step seven assigns the pilot
group in the admin center,

118
00:08:03.943 --> 00:08:06.058
as an Application Administrator.

119
00:08:06.058 --> 00:08:10.012
Step eight turns on signaling and
records the setting to a file;

120
00:08:10.012 --> 00:08:12.446
signaling status should read enabled.

121
00:08:12.446 --> 00:08:14.470
Step nine is the validation.

122
00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:18.304
On the pilot device, sign in to
SharePoint with the client running,

123
00:08:18.304 --> 00:08:22.920
then disable the client from the tray and
sign in again in a new browser session.

124
00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:27.933
With source I P restoration, the two
sign-ins show the same I P address.

125
00:08:27.933 --> 00:08:29.357
Re-enable the client.

126
00:08:29.357 --> 00:08:33.048
Then, in the workspace, run
the guide's sign-in query:

127
00:08:33.048 --> 00:08:37.458
P C T through G S A is the share
of sign-ins the service carried.

128
00:08:37.458 --> 00:08:40.233
Run Module 1's freshness query again too.

129
00:08:40.233 --> 00:08:44.570
Keep the profile and signaling
on; Module 3 needs them.

130
00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.931
The federal requirement, from NIST special

131
00:08:50.931 --> 00:08:54.195
publication eight hundred
fifty-three, revision five.

132
00:08:54.195 --> 00:08:57.963
The client supports C M six,
C M seven and S I four:

133
00:08:57.963 --> 00:09:03.120
managed devices carry the client
and can't silently turn it off.

134
00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:06.947
The evidence is the Intune app's
assignment and detection rule,

135
00:09:06.947 --> 00:09:10.258
the remediation results, and
the device usage summary.

136
00:09:10.258 --> 00:09:15.786
The Microsoft traffic profile supports
A C seventeen, A U three and S I four:

137
00:09:15.786 --> 00:09:19.955
Microsoft three sixty-five
and Entra traffic acquired,

138
00:09:19.955 --> 00:09:22.946
and sign-ins carrying the real source I P.

139
00:09:22.946 --> 00:09:26.525
The evidence is the profile
export and its assignments,

140
00:09:26.525 --> 00:09:29.482
the signaling GET, and
the sign-in query result.

141
00:09:29.482 --> 00:09:33.827
Each row lines up with fed-ramp twenty
X indicators, and the program's

142
00:09:33.827 --> 00:09:38.482
mapping lines Step 4 up with tick three
point oh's Remote User Pattern two.

143
00:09:38.482 --> 00:09:42.640
The evidence supports the
controls; the assessor decides.

144
00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.365
Check yourself with two questions.

145
00:09:48.365 --> 00:09:51.658
First: when does the guide
deploy the remediation that

146
00:09:51.658 --> 00:09:55.390
hides the disable button and
restricts non-privileged users?

147
00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:59.089
The answer is b: from ring
two, after confirming nobody

148
00:09:59.089 --> 00:10:03.040
in the pilot needs to disable
the client, as Learn advises.

149
00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:09.115
Second: which profile can acquire Microsoft
three sixty-five and Entra I D traffic?

150
00:10:09.115 --> 00:10:12.565
The answer is a: only the
Microsoft traffic profile.

151
00:10:12.565 --> 00:10:15.377
The Internet Access
profile never acquires it.

152
00:10:15.377 --> 00:10:20.650
The module page has three more questions,
each linked to the unit that answers it.

153
00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:25.225
To sum up.

154
00:10:25.225 --> 00:10:29.460
You packaged the client with Learn's
values, checked it on a pilot device,

155
00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:34.055
counted the devices the service sees,
enabled the Microsoft traffic profile

156
00:10:34.055 --> 00:10:38.075
for the pilot, turned on signaling,
and proved source I P restoration.

157
00:10:38.075 --> 00:10:40.854
The evidence an I S S O
keeps from this module:

158
00:10:40.854 --> 00:10:44.327
the Intune app's assignment
export and detection rule,

159
00:10:44.327 --> 00:10:49.499
the client health check export, the device
usage summary with the coverage ratio,

160
00:10:49.499 --> 00:10:53.204
the profile export and its
assignments, the signaling GET,

161
00:10:53.204 --> 00:10:56.137
the source I P comparison,
and the sign-in share.

162
00:10:56.137 --> 00:11:00.428
Next is Module 3, the compliant
network and tenant restrictions,

163
00:11:00.428 --> 00:11:04.151
the two signals only Entra
can produce from the network,

164
00:11:04.151 --> 00:11:07.770
run in report-only or a pilot
before they block anyone.
